WEBVTT

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:15.200
<b><i>Planet With</i></b>

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:33.480
Torai-san, how are you doing?

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:37.110
Oh, is that you, Takatori?

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:41.620
<b>Episode 8: Power Is What Dwells Within Your Own Self</b>

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:38.820
Sleep deprived, honestly.

00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:42.300
There's a lot of work to do,
checking out the damaged areas and things.

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:45.120
Well, it beats having nothing to do.

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:47.900
Any interest in rebuilding Grand Paladin?

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:49.670
You know that's impossible.

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:51.070
I don't have my vial,

00:01:51.070 --> 00:01:54.710
and I don't know how to 
identify other psychic humans.

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:58.930
How did Director Ryuzoji do it?

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:03.810
When he came to me, he was 
carrying dowsing rods.

00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:03.810
<b>Metropolitan Police Department</b>

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:05.520
Dowsing rods?

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.420
What happened to the vial I left behind?

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:11.520
It was given to a lab after 
the director vanished.

00:02:11.910 --> 00:02:14.880
But two days ago it was stolen 
by a girl wearing goth loli fashion

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:16.820
who came in from a seventh-story window.

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:18.450
They don't try to hide, do they?

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:22.160
We still don't know what 
that sand inside it is.

00:02:23.090 --> 00:02:24.640
Hey, Torai-san...

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:26.620
About that thing we discussed.

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:28.730
Oh, that.

00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:30.370
No thanks.

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:33.290
I'm not joining the Sealing Faction.

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:39.990
Well, true...

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:43.600
The role of traitor to humanity 
isn't one that suits you.

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:44.890
You're a nice guy.

00:02:45.050 --> 00:02:46.610
What does that mean?

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:49.160
I don't have my vial, anyway.

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:50.640
I can't be your ally or your enemy.

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:53.810
The vials were just the 
key to unlock our powers.

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:56.110
They weren't our powers' source.

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:00.730
I can't go back now.

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:03.360
Torai-san, be careful.

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:05.160
Psychics are dangerous.

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:07.330
Wait, Takatori...

00:03:09.170 --> 00:03:09.960
Takatori!

00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:12.410
Farewell.

00:03:15.130 --> 00:03:16.140
What was that?

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:17.090
I saw a light!

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:19.300
Did something just fly away?

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:22.630
Kuroi-kun...

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:27.600
I-Is there anywhere you'd want to go today?

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:28.950
Today?

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:30.340
What about the occult research club?

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:33.090
We're not going.

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:34.670
Remember?

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:38.100
We were gonna go somewhere 
after school today!

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:39.150
We said that yesterday!

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:42.890
Yeah.

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:46.780
So, if there's no other
 place you'd want to go...

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:48.990
<b>Soramisaka Aquarium</b>

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:51.120
<b>Closed Today</b>

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:55.130
I should've checked.

00:03:55.130 --> 00:03:57.840
"Closed in light of the 
potential stress to the fish

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:01.090
Closed in light of the potential stress to the fish after the damage to the surrounding area.
Soramisaka Aquarium Director

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:01.090
after the damage to the surrounding area."

00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:05.340
It's one of the few tourist 
spots in the town, too.

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:06.830
This is my fault, isn't it?

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:09.680
It's not your fault, Kuroi-kun.

00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:13.390
H-How can you be sure?

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:17.110
Because you protected the town, right?

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:19.550
I did not.

00:04:19.550 --> 00:04:20.990
I can tell.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:23.700
Somehow, I could tell.

00:04:24.270 --> 00:04:27.970
I could tell that you protected the town.

00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:34.460
So I wanted you to see all the best 
parts of the town you protected.

00:04:35.010 --> 00:04:36.250
Sorry.

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:39.790
No, it's fine.

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:43.080
Wh-Why don't we just take a walk instead?

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:44.480
Okay.

00:04:48.590 --> 00:04:51.610
You're a nice person, Nozo-san.

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:52.970
What?

00:04:52.970 --> 00:04:54.280
Is that a compliment?

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:17.580
What's going on here?

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:20.620
Those kids are on a date!

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:22.550
It's so bittersweet!

00:05:22.810 --> 00:05:25.980
Listen, Shiraishi-san, 
are we still doing this?

00:05:25.980 --> 00:05:27.800
There's no point in watching them.

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:31.310
Oh, you can't fight your 
enemy unless you know them.

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:33.990
Is that what we're getting out of this?

00:05:34.420 --> 00:05:35.980
I can't just watch this!

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:38.770
I'm going to interfere with their date!

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:41.070
Why?!

00:05:42.660 --> 00:05:45.220
Was Shiraishi-san always like that?

00:05:47.750 --> 00:05:50.910
Um, "Don't worry about Shiraishi."

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:54.630
"She's just cutting loose a little

00:05:54.630 --> 00:05:58.830
since she had to be Takashi Ryuzoji's
 secretary for so long."

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:02.280
You can tell what that dog's saying?

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:04.740
He says, "Call me Generalissimo."

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:06.300
I see.

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:10.930
He says he wants to know more about why you,

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:15.110
Benika Takatori, decided to 
join the sealing faction.

00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:17.180
For the sake of the Earth.

00:06:18.260 --> 00:06:21.430
"I mean in a more personal sense."

00:06:21.430 --> 00:06:25.440
"I'm lending you the few 
sealing devices I have left."

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:30.860
"I want to know more about you."

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:33.050
All I'm hearing is "woof."

00:06:33.050 --> 00:06:35.830
Is he really saying those long sentences?

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:37.830
He is, yes.

00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:46.170
What is this? A hot spring?

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:50.330
"Let's all get naked together."

00:06:51.370 --> 00:06:53.830
You mean I need to make you trust me?

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:54.560
Fine.

00:06:57.530 --> 00:07:00.730
Where do I even begin, though?

00:07:00.930 --> 00:07:02.510
Why do I have to do this?

00:07:02.510 --> 00:07:04.150
Shut up and interpret!

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:07.900
I was a police officer before this.

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:09.940
I joined because I wanted follow 
in the footsteps of someone

00:07:09.940 --> 00:07:11.240
I'd looked up to since I was a child.

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:13.230
Such a girl, right?

00:07:14.250 --> 00:07:19.160
But in the winter of my first year on 
the force, the detective I admired was killed.

00:07:19.850 --> 00:07:21.680
It was a young boy who killed him.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:23.880
The boy had a homemade gun.

00:07:24.520 --> 00:07:27.520
He'd committed robbery and assault.

00:07:27.520 --> 00:07:28.910
He was on the run.

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:33.100
The detective and I found the boy by chance.

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:36.330
He put his hands above his head 
and walked toward the boy,

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:37.990
hoping to make him put the gun down.

00:07:45.140 --> 00:07:49.030
He started to run and kicked 
the gun out of the boy's hands,

00:07:49.590 --> 00:07:51.470
and arrested him.

00:07:53.590 --> 00:07:58.020
He moved so fast that I thought 
the bullets had missed.

00:08:04.280 --> 00:08:06.210
But they hadn't.

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:10.800
He died of blood loss at the hospital.

00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:14.720
What did he say?

00:08:15.670 --> 00:08:17.390
He says that's very sad.

00:08:20.920 --> 00:08:23.850
The boy's guardians all said that he

00:08:24.260 --> 00:08:26.690
"wasn't the kind of boy to 
do something like that."

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:29.400
He was a "gentle, kind child."

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:31.610
And this is what the boy said.

00:08:32.440 --> 00:08:36.590
"As soon as I picked up the gun,
 I felt invincible.

00:08:36.590 --> 00:08:40.380
It was like I was in a dream."

00:08:42.280 --> 00:08:43.680
"I see."

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:48.530
"So your motive comes from a 
hatred of power itself," he says.

00:08:48.530 --> 00:08:49.900
I guess.

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:54.430
I thought I was an adult.

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:58.120
So I thought I'd be okay 
even if I had that power.

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:03.580
But when Kumashiro's armor turned 
into a dragon and she lost control,

00:09:03.980 --> 00:09:07.930
I knew for certain that the 
same could happen to me.

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:14.710
Psychic powers don't have an interface, 
like a gun's grip or trigger.

00:09:15.230 --> 00:09:16.830
Only your own heart.

00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:19.620
I lacked confidence that 
they wouldn't go out of control.

00:09:20.290 --> 00:09:23.660
That's why I gave my vial 
back and left Grand Paladin.

00:09:25.930 --> 00:09:30.040
"But once your power awakened, 
you couldn't get rid of it."

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:33.510
That's right. And that's why I joined you.

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:37.010
The power beginning to awaken 
in the rest of the Earthlings...

00:09:37.460 --> 00:09:41.260
The power of my comrades,
 which may have already awakened...

00:09:41.780 --> 00:09:45.480
My own power, which has already awakened...

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:48.530
I wanted you to seal it all away.

00:09:53.710 --> 00:09:54.830
"Very well."

00:09:54.830 --> 00:09:57.910
"I will give you a sealing device."

00:09:58.100 --> 00:10:02.030
"You can use it whenever you like," he says.

00:10:07.110 --> 00:10:09.850
Okay, Kuroi-kun, is there 
anywhere else you want to go—

00:10:09.850 --> 00:10:12.040
Hold it!

00:10:12.200 --> 00:10:14.130
Fancy seeing you here!

00:10:14.520 --> 00:10:16.260
Where are you two going?

00:10:17.090 --> 00:10:18.440
Her again!

00:10:18.440 --> 00:10:20.210
You're with the Sealing Faction!

00:10:20.210 --> 00:10:21.010
Sealing Faction?

00:10:21.240 --> 00:10:22.590
Now, now...

00:10:22.590 --> 00:10:24.940
Don't worry about that today.

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:27.480
Huh?

00:10:28.010 --> 00:10:29.480
Shiraishi-san?

00:10:30.110 --> 00:10:32.580
K-Kuroi-kun? What's wrong?

00:10:33.330 --> 00:10:35.610
That's right. It doesn't work on her.

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:36.690
What do I do?

00:10:36.950 --> 00:10:40.030
Um, we're leaving.

00:10:40.030 --> 00:10:41.320
Let's go, Kuroi-kun.

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:42.560
Now, now...

00:10:42.560 --> 00:10:43.970
Let me join in the fun.

00:10:43.970 --> 00:10:45.870
Okay, Kuroi-kun?

